@lang en
IMPORT `bm-ear-part2-third-party`

-- The hostile reading: each assertion here demonstrates a finding in NOTES.md section 4.
-- Each asserts the SURPRISING answer the document gives on its words, worked by hand from
-- the text before it was run. These are satisfied assertions about defects in the
-- instrument, not failures of the encoding. Finding numbers follow NOTES.md.

§ `Tests: findings`

§§ `Finding 1: the 14-day bar runs from the occurrence, not from discovery`

-- Damage occurs on 1 June 2026 but is hidden; found on 20 June; notice received 21 June,
-- the day after it was found. Bao Minh is not liable for any of it.
`a latent loss, notified the day after it was found` MEANS
    `the standard claim, with notice received` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 21)) `, assessed on` (YMD 2026 8 1)
#ASSERT `the grounds that defeat the whole of` `a latent loss, notified the day after it was found` EQUALS LIST `GC5: Bao Minh received no notice within 14 days of the occurrence`
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` `a latent loss, notified the day after it was found` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Part II: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` `a latent loss, notified the day after it was found` EQUALS 0

§§ `Finding 2: an innocent, immaterial wrong answer defeats every claim`

-- One answer in the questionnaire was incomplete. The policy asks nothing about intent,
-- materiality or connection with the loss: nothing is payable under either Part.
`a claim after an incomplete answer` MEANS
    `the standard claim, under the policy` (`the standard policy with answers` `given, and at least one answer untrue or incomplete`)
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` `a claim after an incomplete answer` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Part II: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` `a claim after an incomplete answer` EQUALS 0
-- The same claim with true answers pays 900,000,000 under Part I and 330,000,000 under Part II.
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` `the standard claim` EQUALS 900000000
#ASSERT `Part II: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` `the standard claim` EQUALS 330000000

§§ `Finding 3: any breach of any duty defeats the claim, connected or not`

-- The Insured did not follow a manufacturer's recommendation about some other machine; the
-- loss is a crane collapse the recommendation had nothing to do with.
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`the standard claim, by an Insured with` (`a record of the breaches` (LIST `GC3: comply with the manufacturer's rules and recommendations`))) EQUALS 0
-- A late police report of an unrelated theft defeats a Part II claim for an injury.
#ASSERT `Part II: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`the standard claim, by an Insured with` (`a record of the breaches` (LIST `GC5(e): inform the police of a loss by theft`))) EQUALS 0

§§ `Finding 4: General Condition 1 makes Article 1's average redundant`

-- Item 1 underinsured (80%) because the Insured did not raise the sum insured when prices
-- rose. Article 1's own remedy is average (710,000,000); but the undertaking to adjust is
-- a duty, and General Condition 1 makes it a condition precedent: nothing is payable.
`an underinsured claim` MEANS
    `a claim under` (`the standard policy with schedule` `a schedule with underinsured item 1`) `with losses` (LIST `the standard loss`)
`the same claim, with the undertaking recorded as broken` MEANS
    `a claim under` (`the standard policy with schedule` `a schedule with underinsured item 1`)
        `by an Insured with` (`a record of the breaches` (LIST `Article 1: increase or decrease the sum insured when materials, wages or prices fluctuate`))
        `for` `the standard occurrence` `with losses` (LIST `the standard loss`) `and liabilities` EMPTY
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` `an underinsured claim` EQUALS 710000000
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` `the same claim, with the undertaking recorded as broken` EQUALS 0

§§ `Finding 5: the burden-of-proof clause speaks of the wrong party`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the burden of proof where exclusion (a) is alleged by` `Bao Minh`
        BECAUSE "the clause after the general exclusions speaks only of an allegation by the Insured"

§§ `Finding 6: as translated, the three-month bar never reaches a rejected claim that is not arbitrated`

-- Liability denied outright on 1 July 2026 (so not arbitrable under General Condition 7,
-- which takes only disputes about the amount); no proceedings by 1 January 2030.
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 8: the rejected claim is barred` (`the standard claim, with dispute` (`a dispute: amount disputed` FALSE `, rejected` TRUE `, award on` NOTHING `, proceedings on` NOTHING) `, assessed on` (YMD 2030 1 1))

§§ `Finding 7: no award, no action; and nothing compels an appointment`

-- A dispute about the amount, liability admitted; Bao Minh never appoints its arbitrator,
-- so there is no award, and no action lies (the trace in bm-ear-tests-duties.l4 shows the
-- missed appointment has no consequence).
#ASSERT NOT `General Condition 7 does not bar an action against Bao Minh on` (`a dispute: amount disputed` TRUE `, rejected` FALSE `, award on` NOTHING `, proceedings on` NOTHING)

§§ `Finding 8: average has no measure for items other than 1, 2 (and 4)`

#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 1: the proportion of the loss recoverable on` `item 3`
        BECAUSE "Article 1 states the amount that ought to have been insured only for items 1 and 2, and Article 4 for item 4"

§§ `Finding 9: a total loss pays nothing until the Insured has replaced the item itself`

-- Item 1 destroyed, worth 8,000,000,000 before; salvage 500,000,000; the Insured has not
-- yet spent anything on replacement. The insuring clause promises cash at Bao Minh's
-- option, but Article 2 pays only costs "actually incurred", after invoices: nothing.
`a total loss not yet replaced` MEANS
    `a loss of` (`machinery in item` 1) `, which is` `a total loss` `, costing` (`costs: restoring` 0 `, value before` 8000000000 `, salvage` 500000000 `, incurred` 0)
#ASSERT null (`Part I: the grounds on which Bao Minh is not liable for` `a total loss not yet replaced` `in` (`the standard claim, with losses` (LIST `a total loss not yet replaced`)))
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`the standard claim, with losses` (LIST `a total loss not yet replaced`)) EQUALS 0

§§ `Finding 10: surrounding property damaged by construction work falls between the Parts`

-- The principal's building next to the site is damaged by the civil works (construction),
-- not by erection or testing. Article 4 does not reach it; Part II exclusion 3(b) excludes
-- it. Neither Part pays.
`an occurrence from construction work only` MEANS
    `an occurrence on 1 June 2026, on or near the site` TRUE `, connected with erection or testing` FALSE `, connected with construction` TRUE
`the principal's building, as a Part II claim` MEANS
    `a liability for` `loss of or damage to property` `, damages` (JUST 300000000) `, consented costs` 0 `, exclusion facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`the gap claim` MEANS
    `a claim under` `the standard policy` `by an Insured with` `a clean record` `for` `an occurrence from construction work only`
        `with losses` (LIST `the standard surrounding-property loss`) `and liabilities` (LIST `the principal's building, as a Part II claim`)
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` `the gap claim` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Part II: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` `the gap claim` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Part I: the grounds on which Bao Minh is not liable for` `the standard surrounding-property loss` `in` `the gap claim` EQUALS LIST `Article 4: not directly connected with the erection or testing of the insured items`

§§ `Finding 13: a weekend stoppage is a "partial cessation of work"`

-- Theft from the site over a weekend when work had stopped: general exclusion (d).
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`the standard claim, for the occurrence` (`an occurrence on` (YMD 2026 6 6) `caused by` (LIST `theft`, `cessation of work, whole or partial`))) EQUALS 0

§§ `Finding 16: a false declaration in one claim forfeits every claim`

-- A false declaration was used in support of an EARLIER claim; this claim is honest.
#ASSERT `Part I: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`the standard claim, by an Insured with` `a record of a false declaration in an earlier claim`) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Part II: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`the standard claim, by an Insured with` `a record of a false declaration in an earlier claim`) EQUALS 0

§§ `Finding 17: after a condition 2 payment, the Insured's further costs are its own`

-- Bao Minh pays a settlement sum under condition 2; the third party then sues and the
-- Insured defends with Bao Minh's consent. Nothing more is payable under Part II.
#ASSERT `Part II: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`a Part II claim with liabilities` (LIST `the standard injury to a passer-by`) `, condition 2 paid` TRUE `, other insurance` FALSE `, share` NOTHING) EQUALS 0

§§ `Finding 18: General Condition 9 gives no basis for Bao Minh's proportion`

#ASSERT REFUSED `Part II: the amount Bao Minh is liable to pay for` (`a Part II claim with liabilities` (LIST `the standard injury to a passer-by`) `, condition 2 paid` FALSE `, other insurance` TRUE `, share` NOTHING)
        BECAUSE "General Condition 9 does not say how Bao Minh's proportion is computed, and none has been agreed or determined"
